WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.578
ALEXIS MOUSSINE-POUCHKINE:
Firebase

00:00:01.578 --> 00:00:04.190
is Google's mobile and web
app development platform

00:00:04.190 --> 00:00:06.660
and it offers many
useful cloud services.

00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:10.230
So you might wonder, what is the
relationship between Firebase

00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:11.885
and Google Cloud Platform?

00:00:11.885 --> 00:00:13.635
Stick around and I'll
help you understand.

00:00:13.635 --> 00:00:17.180
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:21.830
You may know Firebase
for all the features

00:00:21.830 --> 00:00:24.120
it offers to enhance
your client app,

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:27.980
such as authentication,
analytics, crash reporting, AB

00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:30.050
testing, or in-app messaging.

00:00:30.050 --> 00:00:32.180
But Firebase also
has several options

00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:35.060
to manage data and
business logic in the cloud

00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:37.250
to help you build better apps.

00:00:37.250 --> 00:00:41.090
This includes a No SQL
database, server-less functions,

00:00:41.090 --> 00:00:43.130
on device and server
side machine learning

00:00:43.130 --> 00:00:45.710
APIs, blob storage, and more.

00:00:45.710 --> 00:00:47.630
Firebase is a wonderful
way for Android

00:00:47.630 --> 00:00:50.750
and web developers to
leverage Google Cloud Services

00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:53.960
without exposing them to all
the knobs and dials of GCP.

00:00:53.960 --> 00:00:56.970
In fact, when you create
a Firebase project,

00:00:56.970 --> 00:00:59.780
it is a GCP project
in every aspect.

00:00:59.780 --> 00:01:02.900
Resource grouping, identity
management, and billing,

00:01:02.900 --> 00:01:03.950
are all the same.

00:01:03.950 --> 00:01:06.650
This gives you a great way
to start using some cloud

00:01:06.650 --> 00:01:09.770
services before you
graduate into using GCP only

00:01:09.770 --> 00:01:10.700
when you need to.

00:01:10.700 --> 00:01:12.650
This is also
important to any user

00:01:12.650 --> 00:01:15.740
interested in building a
mobile or web app on top

00:01:15.740 --> 00:01:17.810
of an existing GCP
infrastructure.

00:01:17.810 --> 00:01:20.720
While the look and feel of
the Firebase console and cloud

00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:24.050
console are clearly different,
you can open the same project

00:01:24.050 --> 00:01:25.050
with either one.

00:01:25.050 --> 00:01:26.870
If you'd like to
open an existing GCP

00:01:26.870 --> 00:01:30.260
project in the Firebase console
to add Firebase-specific

00:01:30.260 --> 00:01:33.680
functionality, simply
select add a project

00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:36.020
and click through
the few setup steps.

00:01:36.020 --> 00:01:39.950
Once done, all the Firebase APIs
will be automatically enabled

00:01:39.950 --> 00:01:40.940
in your project.

00:01:40.940 --> 00:01:42.860
If you have an existing
Firebase project,

00:01:42.860 --> 00:01:45.140
simply head over
to Cloud Console

00:01:45.140 --> 00:01:47.570
and open it there
with its identifier.

00:01:47.570 --> 00:01:49.820
You should see and
be able to manipulate

00:01:49.820 --> 00:01:51.750
all of the project resources.

00:01:51.750 --> 00:01:54.710
Finally, you want to be
careful about deleting projects

00:01:54.710 --> 00:01:56.870
as deleting a Firebase
project deletes

00:01:56.870 --> 00:01:59.750
the Google Cloud
projects as well and all

00:01:59.750 --> 00:02:01.740
its contained resources.

00:02:01.740 --> 00:02:04.850
So now that you know that
a Firebase project is also

00:02:04.850 --> 00:02:08.389
GCP project, let's focus
on the three main products

00:02:08.389 --> 00:02:10.430
that Firebase and
GCP have in common.

00:02:10.430 --> 00:02:14.230
Cloud storage, a massively
scalable blob storage system,

00:02:14.230 --> 00:02:17.120
Cloud Functions, a server-less
compute infrastructure

00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:20.840
for event driven programming,
and Cloud Firestore,

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:24.030
a massively scalable
no SQL database.

00:02:24.030 --> 00:02:26.630
These three GCP products
can be used in Firebase

00:02:26.630 --> 00:02:30.290
with additional mobile SDKs,
as well as from the Firebase

00:02:30.290 --> 00:02:33.410
CLI or command line interface.

00:02:33.410 --> 00:02:36.290
We'll cover the first
one now and the other two

00:02:36.290 --> 00:02:37.470
in the next video.

00:02:37.470 --> 00:02:39.530
So make sure you
subscribe to this channel.

00:02:39.530 --> 00:02:42.950
Cloud storage is a powerful,
yet simple to use blob

00:02:42.950 --> 00:02:44.362
storage system.

00:02:44.362 --> 00:02:46.070
And if you have not
heard of it, then you

00:02:46.070 --> 00:02:49.220
should check out the short data
and storage overview video link

00:02:49.220 --> 00:02:49.760
below.

00:02:49.760 --> 00:02:52.940
Cloud console exposes the
full power of cloud storage

00:02:52.940 --> 00:02:55.940
while the Firebase console
exposes those features that

00:02:55.940 --> 00:02:58.700
are most likely to be relevant
to Firebase developers.

00:02:58.700 --> 00:03:01.970
A typical use case for Firebase
developers using cloud storage

00:03:01.970 --> 00:03:05.310
is when managing user
generated content.

00:03:05.310 --> 00:03:08.930
This is where the Firebase
Android, iOS, web, Unity,

00:03:08.930 --> 00:03:13.610
and c++ SDKs, make it easy
and yet secure to upload

00:03:13.610 --> 00:03:17.690
and download objects such as
images straight from the app.

00:03:17.690 --> 00:03:20.600
Similarly to GCP projects
using App Engine,

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:23.840
any new Firebase project comes
with a default cloud storage

00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:24.560
bucket.

00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:26.870
In most cases,
Firebase developers

00:03:26.870 --> 00:03:29.600
also use this default
storage location

00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:31.760
and does not need to
reference it by name.

00:03:31.760 --> 00:03:34.710
Because of all the GCP
and Firebase commonalities

00:03:34.710 --> 00:03:37.760
this causes so far, any
data stored in Cloud Storage

00:03:37.760 --> 00:03:40.160
using Firebase can
be further access

00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:43.400
and processed in
GCB and vise versa.

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:45.395
Imagine, for
instance, a Firebase

00:03:45.395 --> 00:03:47.870
powered mobile applications
uploading pictures

00:03:47.870 --> 00:03:49.520
to cloud storage.

00:03:49.520 --> 00:03:52.700
It would be quite easy for
a Cloud Scheduler initiate

00:03:52.700 --> 00:03:56.360
a task to resize, crop,
delete, or otherwise

00:03:56.360 --> 00:03:59.570
manipulate all pictures
in this default bucket.

00:03:59.570 --> 00:04:03.260
You can also feed these
files into other GCP big data

00:04:03.260 --> 00:04:08.180
products such as BigQuery, data
flow, or even into our machine

00:04:08.180 --> 00:04:09.530
learning products.

00:04:09.530 --> 00:04:11.600
One thing that you
will want to note

00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:15.830
is how bucket access control
is different and orthogonal.

00:04:15.830 --> 00:04:19.790
Cloud IAM is used to control
access to buckets and objects

00:04:19.790 --> 00:04:22.140
from GCP services.

00:04:22.140 --> 00:04:25.010
On the other hand,
Firebase security rules

00:04:25.010 --> 00:04:27.800
control access only
from mobile applications

00:04:27.800 --> 00:04:29.720
that use the Firebase SDKs.

00:04:29.720 --> 00:04:33.530
So there, you now know how
data stored in Cloud Storage

00:04:33.530 --> 00:04:36.710
can be equally accessed
via a Firebase powered app

00:04:36.710 --> 00:04:40.190
as well as you know from
your GCP hosted applications.

00:04:40.190 --> 00:04:42.950
In the next episode, we'll
discuss the two remaining

00:04:42.950 --> 00:04:46.760
products common to both
platforms, Cloud Functions

00:04:46.760 --> 00:04:48.230
and Cloud Firestore.

00:04:48.230 --> 00:04:50.690
Same project and
building infrastructure,

00:04:50.690 --> 00:04:52.220
common cloud storage.

00:04:52.220 --> 00:04:54.650
The two platforms
have a lot in common

00:04:54.650 --> 00:04:57.860
and were conceived to nicely
complement one another.

00:04:57.860 --> 00:05:02.240
It's time to get going with
Firebase or GCP or both.

00:05:02.240 --> 00:05:04.020
Thanks for watching this video.

00:05:04.020 --> 00:05:07.310
Please like, subscribe,
comment, share, and look forward

00:05:07.310 --> 00:05:08.960
to more GCP Essentials videos.

00:05:08.960 --> 00:05:12.010
[MUSIC PLAYING]

